   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Gender transofmative programming prototypes in number of countries piloted. 
- Gender solutions prototypes communicated. 
- Number of policy guidance tools are completed.
- Number of ender equality tool for private sector. 

Only for 2021: Regional policy dialogue on gender integration in socioecnomic response to COVID19 conducted. 
Only for 2021: Gender mainstreaming learning tool rolled out in COs</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">0
At least one event
0
0

2021 indicators:
No such dialogue undertaken. 
A previous guidance note on gender mainstreaming exists which has been updated but not rolled out.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Solution prototypes in 5 countries to be completed. 
- Insights and learnings from the solutions prototypes communicated. 
- Country offices are supported to mobilize resources and create partnerships to continue the work on addressing gender inequalities in the context of future of work.
- Number of policy guidance pilots are completed.
- 1 gender equality tool for private sector.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Solution prototypes in 5 countries have been completed and ready to scale. 
- Insights and learnings from the solutions prototypes are showcased at the Gender CoP regional meeting. 
- Country offices are supported to mobilize resources and create partnerships to continue the work on addressing gender inequalities in the context of future of work.
- Unpaid care policy guidance pilots are completed and serve to inform the revision of the policy guidance note.
- The design of the Sustainable Development Services Gender Equality tool for private sector is complete and has initiated a pilot phase.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Financing tools and methodologies for gender equality prototyped. 

- Gender transformative programming prototypes piloted.

- Tools to support gender transformative programming developed.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Two financing tools under development in Mongolia and China 
 - A mechanism to support capacity development and marketing of women-owned green businesses piloted in Bangladesh.
- A time use survey methodology is developed and tested in Samoa. Behaviourial change guidance note developed in India to address unpaid care work. 
-Gender mainstreaming learning tool has been implemented in Thailand, Maldives, Cambodia,Samoa, Fiji, Indonesia,Sri lanka, Lao PDR, Bangladesh, China, Iran, Pakistan</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Policy guidance on unpaid care work to be implemented in at least one country. 
Sustainable Development Services Gender Equality diversity and inclusion rolled out wit at least one partner.

Only for 2021 - Regional policy dialogue on gender integration in socioecnomic response to COVID19 conducted. 
Only for 2021: Gender mainstreaming learning tool rolled out in COs</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Policy guidance on unpaid care work has been used as a research framework in Thailand. But the research has not turned into policy options yet. 

Sustainable Development Services Gender Equality Diversity and Inclusion has been rolled out in Bhutan with the Bhutan Chamber of Commerce and Industry. 

No Regional policy dialogue on gender integration in socioeconomic response to COVID19 was organised in 2021. 

2. Gender mainstreaming learning tool has been rolled out, and Samoa CO is using it right now. Other COS have plans to use it in 2022</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
